 users will be cautious about their safety."], "answer": 0, "image": null, "explanation": "The published Parivahan question bank identifies “Driving cautiously anticipating violation of trafficrules and road signs both by drivers and other road users.” as the correct answer.", "source_url": "https://parivahan.gov.in/sites/default/files/DownloadForm/STALL_QB_ENGLISH_NEW.pdf", "source_ref": "Question 171, PDF page 13", "imported_at": "2026-10-23", "topic": "Safe driving"}, {"id": "parivahan-180", "category": "rules", "prompt": "When lorries are loaded…", "options": ["The load can be projected to both sides within 30 cm.", "The load shall not project on both sides.", "The load can be projected to both sides within 50 cm."], "answer": 1, "image": null, "explanation": "The published Parivahan question bank identifies “The load shall not project on both sides.” as the correct answer.", "source_url": "https://parivahan.gov.in/sites/default/files/DownloadForm/STALL_QB_ENGLISH_NEW.pdf", "source_ref": "Question 180, PDF page 14", "imported_at": "2026-10-23", "topic": "Safe driving"}, {"id": "parivahan-190", "category": "rules", "prompt": "Maximum permitted weight that can be carried on a goods carriage….", "options": ["No limit", "allowed as per permit", "10 ton"], "answer": 1, "image": null, "explanation": "The published Parivahan question bank identifies “allowed as per permit” as the correct answer.", "source_url": "https://parivahan.gov.in/sites/default/files/DownloadForm/STALL_QB_ENGLISH_NEW.pdf", "source_ref": "Question 190, PDF page 14", "imported_at": "2026-10-23", "topic": "Safe driving"}, {"id": "parivahan-199", "category": "rules", "prompt": "According to section 112 of the Motor Vehicles Act 1988…", "options": ["Speed limit shall not be exceeded", "Shall not drive after consuming alcohol", "Shall not use vehicle on road without paying tax"], "answer": 0, "image": null, "explanation": "The published Parivahan question bank identifies “Speed limit shall not be exceeded” as the correct answer.", "source_url": "https://parivahan.gov.in/sites/default/files/DownloadForm/STALL_QB_ENGLISH_NEW.pdf", "source_ref": "Question 199, PDF page 15", "imported_at": "2026-10-23", "topic": "Safe driving"}, {"id": "parivahan-200", "category": "rules", "prompt": "Section 113 of the Motor Vehicle Act 1988 stipulates that the driver should not drive a vehicle…..", "options": ["After consuming alcohol.", "Exceeding the speed limit", "Exceeding the weight permitted to carry"], "answer": 2, "image": null, "explanation": "The published Parivahan question bank identifies “Exceeding the weight permitted to carry” as the correct answer.", "source_url": "https://parivahan.gov.in/sites/default/files/DownloadForm/STALL_QB_ENGLISH_NEW.pdf", "source_ref": "Question 200, PDF page 15", "imported_at": "2026-10-23", "topic": "Safe driving"}, {"id": "parivahan-205", "category": "rules", "prompt": "According to section 129 of Motor Vehicle Act 1988 a person driving a motor cycle shall….", "options": ["wear jerkins", "wear helmet", "wear shoes"], "answer": 1, "image": null, "explanation": "The published Parivahan question bank identifies “wear helmet” as the correct answer.", "source_url": "https://parivahan.gov.in/sites/default/files/DownloadForm/STALL_QB_ENGLISH_NEW.pdf", "source_ref": "Question 205, PDF page 15", "imported_at": "2026-10-23", "topic": "Safe driving"}, {"id": "parivahan-213", "category": "rules", "prompt": "Zig-Zag driving is….", "options": ["Dangerous to two-wheelers only", "Dangerous to all at all times", "Dangerous to four- wheelers vehicles"], "answer": 1, "image": null, "explanation": "The published Parivahan question bank identifies “Dangerous to all at all times” as the correct answer.", "source_url": "https://parivahan.gov.in/sites/default/files/DownloadForm/STALL_QB_ENGLISH_NEW.pdf", "source_ref": "Question 213, PDF page 15", "imported_at": "2026-10-23", "topic": "Safe driving"}, {"id": "parivahan-214", "category": "rules", "prompt": "You are on a long downhill slope. What should you do to help control the speed of your vehicle ?", "options": ["change to low gear", "Stop the Engine", "select neutral"], "answer": 0, "image": null, "explanation": "The published Parivahan question bank identifies “change to low gear” as the correct answer.", "source_url": "https://parivahan.gov.in/sites/default/files/DownloadForm/STALL_QB_ENGLISH_NEW.pdf", "source_ref": "Question 214, PDF page 15", "imported_at": "2026-10-23", "topic": "Safe driving"}, {"id": "parivahan-216", "category": "rules", "prompt": "While on a round about", "options": ["traffic entering has right of way", "traffic existing has right of way", "traffic on the roundabout has right of way"], "answer": 2, "image": null, "explanation": "The published Parivahan question bank identifies “traffic on the roundabout has right of way” as the correct answer.", "source_url": "https://parivahan.gov.in/sites/default/files/DownloadForm/STALL_QB_ENGLISH_NEW.pdf", "source_ref": "Question 216, PDF page 15", "imported_at": "2026-10-23", "topic": "Safe driving"}, {"id": "parivahan-217", "category": "rules", "prompt": "It is essential to wear a helmet while driving a two- wheeler because….", "options": ["It is for your individual safety", "Otherwise you will be caught by the traffic police", "It is necessary for uniformity on the road"], "answer": 0, "image": null, "explanation": "The published Parivahan question bank identifies “It is for your individual safety” as the correct answer.", "source_url": "https://parivahan.gov.in/sites/default/files/DownloadForm/STALL_QB_ENGLISH_NEW.pdf", "source_ref": "Question 217, PDF page 15", "imported_at": "2026-10-23", "topic": "Safe driving"}, {"id": "parivahan-219", "category": "rules", "prompt": "You are behind a bus that has stopped to pickup or drop off passengers you should…..", "options": ["wait behind patiently", "overtake from the left", "overtake from the pedestrians"], "answer": 0, "image": null, "explanation": "The published Parivahan question bank identifies “wait behind patiently” as the correct answer.", "source_url": "https://parivahan.gov.in/sites/default/files/DownloadForm/STALL_QB_ENGLISH_NEW.pdf", "source_ref": "Question 219, PDF page 16", "imported_at": "2026-10-23", "topic": "Safe driving"}, {"id": "parivahan-222", "category": "rules", "prompt": "A flashing yellow signal is used when…..", "options": ["traffic lights aren’t working", "you should slow down & proceed with caution", "men are at work"], "answer": 1, "image": null, "explanation": "The published Parivahan question bank identifies “you should slow down & proceed with caution” as the correct answer.", "source_url": "https://parivahan.gov.in/sites/default/files/DownloadForm/STALL_QB_ENGLISH_NEW.pdf", "source_ref": "Question 222, PDF page 16", "imported_at": "2026-10-23", "topic": "Safe driving"}, {"id": "parivahan-223", "category": "rules", "prompt": "You stop for pedestrians waiting to cross at a zebra crossing. They do not start to cross. What should you do ?", "options": ["sound your horn", "be patient and wait", "drive on"], "answer": 1, "image": null, "explanation": "The published Parivahan question bank identifies “be patient and wait” as the correct answer.", "source_url": "https://parivahan.gov.in/sites/default/files/DownloadForm/STALL_QB_ENGLISH_NEW.pdf", "source_ref": "Question 223, PDF page 16", "imported_at": "2026-10-23", "topic": "Safe driving"}, {"id": "parivahan-225", "category": "rules", "prompt": "A high beam in foggy conditions….", "options": ["is good because you can see more", "is bad because it reflects back and can dazzle", "make sure others can see you"], "answer": 1, "image": null, "explanation": "The published Parivahan question bank identifies “is bad because it reflects back and can dazzle” as the correct answer.", "source_url": "https://parivahan.gov.in/sites/default/files/DownloadForm/STALL_QB_ENGLISH_NEW.pdf", "source_ref": "Question 225, PDF page 16", "imported_at": "2026-10-23", "topic": "Safe driving"}, {"id": "parivahan-228", "category": "rules", "prompt": "You are driving. A vehicle comes up quickly behind, flashing head lamps. You should…..", "options": ["accelerate to maintain gap behind you", "touch the breaks to show your brake lights", "allow the vehicle to over take, if safe"], "answer": 2, "image": null, "explanation": "The published Parivahan question bank identifies “allow the vehicle to over take, if safe” as the correct answer.", "source_url": "https://parivahan.gov.in/sites/default/files/DownloadForm/STALL_QB_ENGLISH_NEW.pdf", "source_ref": "Question 228, PDF page 16", "imported_at": "2026-10-23", "topic": "Safe driving"}, {"id": "parivahan-230", "category": "rules", "prompt": "You are driving in rain. Why should you keep well back from the vehicle in front ?", "options": ["in case it changes direction suddenly", "in case its fog lights dazzle you", "in case it stop suddenly"], "answer": 2, "image": null, "explanation": "The published Parivahan question bank identifies “in case it stop suddenly” as the correct answer.", "source_url": "https://parivahan.gov.in/sites/default/files/DownloadForm/STALL_QB_ENGLISH_NEW.pdf", "source_ref": "Question 230, PDF page 16", "imported_at": "2026-10-23", "topic": "Safe driving"}, {"id": "parivahan-231", "category": "rules", "prompt": "What can cause hard steering", "options": ["badly worn tyre", "over inflated tyre", "under inflated tyre"], "answer": 2, "image": null, "explanation": "The published Parivahan question bank identifies “under inflated tyre” as the correct answer.", "source_url": "https://parivahan.gov.in/sites/default/files/DownloadForm/STALL_QB_ENGLISH_NEW.pdf", "source_ref": "Question 231, PDF page 16", "imported_at": "2026-10-23", "topic": "Safe driving"}, {"id": "parivahan-234", "category": "rules", "prompt": "While you reach a junction with limited visibility you should", "options": ["look both ways and move carefully", "look at right and move slowly", "move quickly"], "answer": 0, "image": null, "explanation": "The published Parivahan question bank identifies “look both ways and move carefully” as the correct answer.", "source_url": "https://parivahan.gov.in/sites/default/files/DownloadForm/STALL_QB_ENGLISH_NEW.pdf", "source_ref": "Question 234, PDF page 16", "imported_at": "2026-10-23", "topic": "Safe driving"}, {"id": "parivahan-236", "category": "rules", "prompt": "You are driving on a well-lit motor way at night, you must", "options": ["use your head light on high beam", "always use your head lights in low beam", "always use hazard light"], "answer": 1, "image": null, "explanation": "The published Parivahan question bank identifies “always use your head lights in low beam” as the correct answer.", "source_url": "https://parivahan.gov.in/sites/default/files/DownloadForm/STALL_QB_ENGLISH_NEW.pdf", "source_ref": "Question 236, PDF page 16", "imported_at": "2026-10-23", "topic": "Safe driving"}, {"id": "parivahan-237", "category": "rules", "prompt": "Anti lock braking system prevents wheels from locking. This avoid tyres to", "options": ["Puncture", "skid", "wear"], "answer": 1, "image": null, "explanation": "The published Parivahan question bank identifies “skid” as the correct answer.", "source_url": "https://parivahan.gov.in/sites/default/files/DownloadForm/STALL_QB_ENGLISH_NEW.pdf", "source_ref": "Question 237, PDF page 16", "imported_at": "2026-10-23", "topic": "Safe driving"}, {"id": "parivahan-238", "category": "rules", "prompt": "While travelling over motor way at night with other vehicles just ahead, better the switched on lights should be", "options": ["hazard warning light", "low beam head light", "high beam head light"], "answer": 1, "image": null, "explanation": "The published Parivahan question bank identifies “low beam head light” as the correct answer.", "source_url": "https://parivahan.gov.in/sites/default/files/DownloadForm/STALL_QB_ENGLISH_NEW.pdf", "source_ref": "Question 238, PDF page 16", "imported_at": "2026-10-23", "topic": "Safe driving"}, {"id": "parivahan-240", "category": "rules", "prompt": "Driving at high speed", "options": ["gives you better fuel efficiency", "take less time for your journey", "reduces time to react to hazard"], "answer": 2, "image": null, "explanation": "The published Parivahan question bank identifies “reduces time to react to hazard” as the correct answer.", "source_url": "https://parivahan.gov.in/sites/default/files/DownloadForm/STALL_QB_ENGLISH_NEW.pdf", "source_ref": "Question 240, PDF page 17", "imported_at": "2026-10-23", "topic": "Safe driving"}, {"id": "parivahan-241", "category": "rules", "prompt": "While driving, avoid", "options": ["observing traffic rules", "reacting to wrong behaviour of other drivers", "observing the dash board guages"], "answer": 1, "image": null, "explanation": "The published Parivahan question bank identifies “reacting to wrong behaviour of other drivers” as the correct answer.", "source_url": "https://parivahan.gov.in/sites/default/files/DownloadForm/STALL_QB_ENGLISH_NEW.pdf", "source_ref": "Question 241, PDF page 17", "imported_at": "2026-10-23", "topic": "Safe driving"}, {"id": "parivahan-244", "category": "rules", "prompt": "When you approach a bridge you should", "options": ["slow down and do not over take", "beware of pedestrians", "switch on the head lights"], "answer": 0, "image": null, "explanation": "The published Parivahan question bank identifies “slow down and do not over take” as the correct answer.", "source_url": "https://parivahan.gov.in/sites/default/files/DownloadForm/STALL_QB_ENGLISH_NEW.pdf", "source_ref": "Question 244, PDF page 17", "imported_at": "2026-10-23", "topic": "Safe driving"}, {"id": "parivahan-246", "category": "rules", "prompt": "While you are approaching a staggered junction, You should", "options": ["slow the vehicle", "maintain your speed and sound the horn", "use hazard warning light"], "answer": 0, "image": null, "explanation": "The published Parivahan question bank identifies “slow the vehicle” as the correct answer.", "source_url": "https://parivahan.gov.in/sites/default/files/DownloadForm/STALL_QB_ENGLISH_NEW.pdf", "source_ref": "Question 246, PDF page 17", "imported_at": "2026-10-23", "topic": "Safe driving"}, {"id": "parivahan-247", "category": "rules", "prompt": "At the Blind Junction you must stop", "options": ["only if there is traffic on the main road", "behind the line and move forward slowly as vision improves", "only if you are turning to the right"], "answer": 1, "image": null, "explanation": "The published Parivahan question bank identifies “behind the line and move forward slowly as vision improves” as the correct answer.", "source_url": "https://parivahan.gov.in/sites/default/files/DownloadForm/STALL_QB_ENGLISH_NEW.pdf", "source_ref": "Question 247, PDF page 17", "imported_at": "2026-10-23", "topic": "Safe driving"}, {"id": "parivahan-250", "category": "rules", "prompt": "Approaching a cross road, the driver of the long vehicle ahead of you, signals right and moves to left, You should", "options": ["sound horn and warn the driver", "wait behind the vehicle", "over take on the right hand side"], "answer": 1, "image": null, "explanation": "The published Parivahan question bank identifies “wait behind the vehicle” as the correct answer.", "source_url": "https://parivahan.gov.in/sites/default/files/DownloadForm/STALL_QB_ENGLISH_NEW.pdf", "source_ref": "Question 250, PDF page 17", "imported_at": "2026-10-23", "topic": "Safe driving"}, {"id": "parivahan-251", "category": "rules", "prompt": "Basic rule on a two lane high way is", "options": ["keep to the left lane unless over taking", "keep the lane with the least traffic", "always keep to the right lane at high speed"], "answer": 0, "image": null, "explanation": "The published Parivahan question bank identifies “keep to the left lane unless over taking” as the correct answer.", "source_url": "https://parivahan.gov.in/sites/default/files/DownloadForm/STALL_QB_ENGLISH_NEW.pdf", "source_ref": "Question 251, PDF page 17", "imported_at": "2026-10-23", "topic": "Safe driving"}, {"id": "parivahan-252", "category": "rules", "prompt": "You meet an obstruction on your side of the road, You should", "options": ["move on as you have priority", "accelerate to move quickly", "give way to on coming traffic"], "answer": 2, "image": null, "explanation": "The published Parivahan question bank identifies “give way to on coming traffic” as the correct answer.", "source_url": "https://parivahan.gov.in/sites/default/files/DownloadForm/STALL_QB_ENGLISH_NEW.pdf", "source_ref": "Question 252, PDF page 17", "imported_at": "2026-10-23", "topic": "Safe driving"}, {"id": "parivahan-259", "category": "rules", "prompt": "When you are moving from a parking place, You should", "options": ["use the rear view mirrors, check in the blind spot and give signal", "look around the vehicle", "sound horn and move ahead"], "answer": 0, "image": null, "explanation": "The published Parivahan question bank identifies “use the rear view mirrors, check in the blind spot and give signal” as the correct answer.", "source_url": "https://parivahan.gov.in/sites/default/files/DownloadForm/STALL_QB_ENGLISH_NEW.pdf", "source_ref": "Question 259, PDF page 18", "imported_at": "2026-10-23", "topic": "Safe driving"}, {"id": "parivahan-261", "category": "rules", "prompt": "You are intending to turn left , you should position your vehicle at", "options": ["the middle lane", "the left hand lane", "on the shoulder of the road"], "answer": 1, "image": null, "explanation": "The published Parivahan question bank identifies “the left hand lane” as the correct answer.", "source_url": "https://parivahan.gov.in/sites/default/files/DownloadForm/STALL_QB_ENGLISH_NEW.pdf", "source_ref": "Question 261, PDF page 18", "imported_at": "2026-10-23", "topic": "Safe driving"}, {"id": "parivahan-262", "category": "rules", "prompt": "You are in a wrong lane while approaching a busy Junction you should", "options": ["continue in that lane", "stop until other lane is cleared", "show signal and cut across"], "answer": 0, "image": null, "explanation": "The published Parivahan question bank identifies “continue in that lane” as the correct answer.", "source_url": "https://parivahan.gov.in/sites/default/files/DownloadForm/STALL_QB_ENGLISH_NEW.pdf", "source_ref": "Question 262, PDF page 18", "imported_at": "2026-10-23", "topic": "Safe driving"}, {"id": "parivahan-266", "category": "rules", "prompt": "When approaching from the rear, where two lanes of traffic have stopped at a signal, you should", "options": ["pass all the vehicle and stop in front of them", "stop behind the last vehicle in the appropriate lane", "stop any where"], "answer": 1, "image": null, "explanation": "The published Parivahan question bank identifies “stop behind the last vehicle in the appropriate lane” as the correct answer.", "source_url": "https://parivahan.gov.in/sites/default/files/DownloadForm/STALL_QB_ENGLISH_NEW.pdf", "source_ref": "Question 266, PDF page 18", "imported_at": "2026-10-23", "topic": "Safe driving"}, {"id": "parivahan-267", "category": "rules", "prompt": "Rear Mirror is slightly curved to", "options": ["give a wider field of vision", "cover the blind spot totally", "judge the speed of following vehicle"], "answer": 0, "image": null, "explanation": "The published Parivahan question bank identifies “give a wider field of vision” as the correct answer.", "source_url": "https://parivahan.gov.in/sites/default/files/DownloadForm/STALL_QB_ENGLISH_NEW.pdf", "source_ref": "Question 267, PDF page 18", "imported_at": "2026-10-23", "topic": "Safe driving"}, {"id": "parivahan-270", "category": "rules", "prompt": "Fitment of multi toned horns on a motor vehicle is", "options": ["permitted only in emergency", "an offence under the law as it causes noise pollution", "for avoiding accident"], "answer": 1, "image": null, "explanation": "The published Parivahan question bank identifies “an offence under the law as it causes noise pollution” as the correct answer.", "source_url": "https://parivahan.gov.in/sites/default/files/DownloadForm/STALL_QB_ENGLISH_NEW.pdf", "source_ref": "Question 270, PDF page 18", "imported_at": "2026-10-23", "topic": "Safe driving"}, {"id": "parivahan-271", "category": "rules", "prompt": "Your vehicle pulls to one side while braking, You should", "options": ["change the tyres around", "pump the pedal when braking", "consult your mechanic"], "answer": 2, "image": null, "explanation": "The published Parivahan question bank identifies “consult your mechanic” as the correct answer.", "source_url": "https://parivahan.gov.in/sites/default/files/DownloadForm/STALL_QB_ENGLISH_NEW.pdf", "source_ref": "Question 271, PDF page 18", "imported_at": "2026-10-23", "topic": "Safe driving"}, {"id": "parivahan-274", "category": "rules", "prompt": "What is blind spot", "options": ["An area not seen in your rear view mirrors", "an area not covered by head lights", "an area not covered by the rear view mirror inside your vehicle"], "answer": 0, "image": null, "explanation": "The published Parivahan question bank identifies “An area not seen in your rear view mirrors” as the correct answer.", "source_url": "https://parivahan.gov.in/sites/default/files/DownloadForm/STALL_QB_ENGLISH_NEW.pdf", "source_ref": "Question 274, PDF page 18", "imported_at": "2026-10-23", "topic": "Safe driving"}, {"id": "parivahan-275", "category": "rules", "prompt": "While approaching a road under repair, you comply the permitted speed limit", "options": ["during day time and working is going on", "During night time only", "at all times"], "answer": 2, "image": null, "explanation": "The published Parivahan question bank identifies “at all times” as the correct answer.", "source_url": "https://parivahan.gov.in/sites/default/files/DownloadForm/STALL_QB_ENGLISH_NEW.pdf", "source_ref": "Question 275, PDF page 18", "imported_at": "2026-10-23", "topic": "Safe driving"}, {"id": "parivahan-279", "category": "rules", "prompt": "An accident has just happened and the injured person is lying on the road, you should", "options": ["protect the area and inform the authorities", "protect the area and give first aid to injured", "protect the area, give first aid ,take the injured to the hospital and inform the authorities"], "answer": 2, "image": null, "explanation": "The published Parivahan question bank identifies “protect the area, give first aid ,take the injured to the hospital and inform the authorities” as the correct answer.", "source_url": "https://parivahan.gov.in/sites/default/files/DownloadForm/STALL_QB_ENGLISH_NEW.pdf", "source_ref": "Question 279, PDF page 19", "imported_at": "2026-10-23", "topic": "Safe driving"}, {"id": "parivahan-280", "category": "rules", "prompt": "What is the main aim of the first aid", "options": ["To treat the injury", "To prevent aggravating the injury and its effects", "all of the above"], "answer": 1, "image": null, "explanation": "The published Parivahan question bank identifies “To prevent aggravating the injury and its effects” as the correct answer.", "source_url": "https://parivahan.gov.in/sites/default/files/DownloadForm/STALL_QB_ENGLISH_NEW.pdf", "source_ref": "Question 280, PDF page 19", "imported_at": "2026-10-23", "topic": "Safe driving"}, {"id": "parivahan-281", "category": "rules", "prompt": "How does alcohol affect your driving", "options": ["It increase your awareness", "it reduce your concentration and attention", "it increase your confidence"], "answer": 1, "image": null, "explanation": "The published Parivahan question bank identifies “it reduce your concentration and attention” as the correct answer.", "source_url": "https://parivahan.gov.in/sites/default/files/DownloadForm/STALL_QB_ENGLISH_NEW.pdf", "source_ref": "Question 281, PDF page 19", "imported_at": "2026-10-23", "topic": "Safe driving"}, {"id": "parivahan-282", "category": "rules", "prompt": "Which of these lights will come after Amber at a traffic light", "options": ["Red", "Green", "red or greeen"], "answer": 0, "image": null, "explanation": "The published Parivahan question bank identifies “Red” as the correct answer.", "source_url": "https://parivahan.gov.in/sites/default/files/DownloadForm/STALL_QB_ENGLISH_NEW.pdf", "source_ref": "Question 282, PDF page 19", "imported_at": "2026-10-23", "topic": "Safe driving"}, {"id": "parivahan-283", "category": "rules", "prompt": "While driving you start feeling tired or unable to concentrate, You should", "options": ["Stop as soon as it is safe to do so and take rest", "switch on the stereo to help you concentrate", "speed up to get your destination sooner"], "answer": 0, "image": null, "explanation": "The published Parivahan question bank identifies “Stop as soon as it is safe to do so and take rest” as the correct answer.", "source_url": "https://parivahan.gov.in/sites/default/files/DownloadForm/STALL_QB_ENGLISH_NEW.pdf", "source_ref": "Question 283, PDF page 19", "imported_at": "2026-10-23", "topic": "Safe driving"}, {"id": "parivahan-284", "category": "rules", "prompt": "You are drivng at night, what can you do to help you to keep alert?", "options": ["takes proper rest periods at correct intervals", "walk around in fresh air after a rest stop", "both of the above"], "answer": 1, "image": null, "explanation": "The published Parivahan question bank identifies “walk around in fresh air after a rest stop” as the correct answer.", "source_url": "https://parivahan.gov.in/sites/default/files/DownloadForm/STALL_QB_ENGLISH_NEW.pdf", "source_ref": "Question 284, PDF page 19", "imported_at": "2026-10-23", "topic": "Safe driving"}, {"id": "parivahan-285", "category": "rules", "prompt": "You are driving a car during a journey you are feeling ill and unable to concentrate, what should you do?", "options": ["increase your speed to finish your work earlier", "continue your journey and keep your windows open", "stop in a safe place and if possible seek for medical attention"], "answer": 2, "image": null, "explanation": "The published Parivahan question bank identifies “stop in a safe place and if possible seek for medical attention” as the correct answer.", "source_url": "https://parivahan.gov.in/sites/default/files/DownloadForm/STALL_QB_ENGLISH_NEW.pdf", "source_ref": "Question 285, PDF page 19", "imported_at": "2026-10-23", "topic": "Safe driving"}, {"id": "parivahan-286", "category": "rules", "prompt": "Anti lock braking system is designed to", "options": ["prevent the driving wheel from spinning", "prevent moisture from building up inside the braking system", "prevent wheels from locking up on braking and avoid skidding of the tyres"], "answer": 2, "image": null, "explanation": "The published Parivahan question bank identifies “prevent wheels from locking up on braking and avoid skidding of the tyres” as the correct answer.", "source_url": "https://parivahan.gov.in/sites/default/files/DownloadForm/STALL_QB_ENGLISH_NEW.pdf", "source_ref": "Question 286, PDF page 19", "imported_at": "2026-10-23", "topic": "Safe driving"}, {"id": "parivahan-287", "category": "rules", "prompt": "What is \"brake fade\"", "options": ["A reduction of air pressure", "smooth progressive braking", "reduction of braking effectiveness"], "answer": 2, "image": null, "explanation": "The published Parivahan question bank identifies “reduction of braking effectiveness” as the correct answer.", "source_url": "https://parivahan.gov.in/sites/default/files/DownloadForm/STALL_QB_ENGLISH_NEW.pdf", "source_ref": "Question 287, PDF page 19", "imported_at": "2026-10-23", "topic": "Safe driving"}, {"id": "parivahan-289", "category": "rules", "prompt": "When stopping on an uphill gradient, one should", "options": ["Hold the vehicle on the clutch", "Hold the vehicle on the foot brake", "Hold the vehicle applying parking brake after stopping"], "answer": 2, "image": null, "explanation": "The published Parivahan question bank identifies “Hold the vehicle applying parking brake after stopping” as the correct answer.", "source_url": "https://parivahan.gov.in/sites/default/files/DownloadForm/STALL_QB_ENGLISH_NEW.pdf", "source_ref": "Question 289, PDF page 19", "imported_at": "2026-10-23", "topic": "Safe driving"}, {"id": "parivahan-290", "category": "rules", "prompt": "You are driving behind a large vehicle, how can you improve your view ahead?", "options": ["Overtake as soon as you can", "Move over to the left", "Stay further back"], "answer": 2, "image": null, "explanation": "The published Parivahan question bank identifies “Stay further back” as the correct answer.", "source_url": "https://parivahan.gov.in/sites/default/files/DownloadForm/STALL_QB_ENGLISH_NEW.pdf", "source_ref": "Question 290, PDF page 19", "imported_at": "2026-10-23", "topic": "Safe driving"}, {"id": "parivahan-294", "category": "rules", "prompt": "How can you avoid harsh driving?", "options": ["gently apply the parking brake", "plan and take earlier action in using brake", "slow down by using gears only"], "answer": 1, "image": null, "explanation": "The published Parivahan question bank identifies “plan and take earlier action in using brake” as the correct answer.", "source_url": "https://parivahan.gov.in/sites/default/files/DownloadForm/STALL_QB_ENGLISH_NEW.pdf", "source_ref": "Question 294, PDF page 19", "imported_at": "2026-10-23", "topic": "Safe driving"}, {"id": "parivahan-297", "category": "rules", "prompt": "Hazard warning lamps may only be used at certain times", "options": ["for going ahead at a junction", "For slowing down the rear vehicle", "for emergency parking especially on high ways and busy roads"], "answer": 2, "image": null, "explanation": "The published Parivahan question bank identifies “for emergency parking especially on high ways and busy roads” as the correct answer.", "source_url": "https://parivahan.gov.in/sites/default/files/DownloadForm/STALL_QB_ENGLISH_NEW.pdf", "source_ref": "Question 297, PDF page 19", "imported_at": "2026-10-23", "topic": "Safe driving"}, {"id": "parivahan-299", "category": "rules", "prompt": "What must you do if your vehicle is involved in an accident?", "options": ["stop at the scene of the accident, give First Aid to the victim if possible and help him to get medical attention", "drive the vehicle to the nearest police station", "inform the insurance authorities at the earliest"], "answer": 0, "image": null, "explanation": "The published Parivahan question bank identifies “stop at the scene of the accident, give First Aid to the victim if possible and help him to get medical attention” as the correct answer.", "source_url": "https://parivahan.gov.in/sites/default/files/DownloadForm/STALL_QB_ENGLISH_NEW.pdf", "source_ref": "Question 299, PDF page 20", "imported_at": "2026-10-23", "topic": "Safe driving"}, {"id": "parivahan-300", "category": "rules", "prompt": "Your vehicle has hit a parked vehicle. The owner of that vehicle could not be traced out at the time, you must", "options": ["drive away from the accident spot and clear the damage at the earliest", "inform the insurance authorities as soon as possible", "inform the police station having jurisdiction over the place in which the accident occurred within 24 hours"], "answer": 2, "image": null, "explanation": "The published Parivahan question bank identifies “inform the police station having jurisdiction over the place in which the accident occurred within 24 hours” as the correct answer.", "source_url": "https://parivahan.gov.in/sites/default/files/DownloadForm/STALL_QB_ENGLISH_NEW.pdf", "source_ref": "Question 300, PDF page 20", "imported_at": "2026-10-23", "topic": "Safe driving"}, {"id": "parivahan-302", "category": "rules", "prompt": "Motor cyclist are advised to wear ------------------------type of clothing at night to make them visible to other road users", "options": ["bright clothing", "dark clothing", "none of this"], "answer": 0, "image": null, "explanation": "The published Parivahan question bank identifies “bright clothing” as the correct answer.", "source_url": "https://parivahan.gov.in/sites/default/files/DownloadForm/STALL_QB_ENGLISH_NEW.pdf", "source_ref": "Question 302, PDF page 20", "imported_at": "2026-10-23", "topic": "Safe driving"}, {"id": "parivahan-303", "category": "rules", "prompt": "Before you open the right side doors on parking, you should", "options": ["ensure that no vehicle is passing by", "quickly open the door and get down", "do not open the right doors and get down through the left only"], "answer": 0, "image": null, "explanation": "The published Parivahan question bank identifies “ensure that no vehicle is passing by” as the correct answer.", "source_url": "https://parivahan.gov.in/sites/default/files/DownloadForm/STALL_QB_ENGLISH_NEW.pdf", "source_ref": "Question 303, PDF page 20", "imported_at": "2026-10-23", "topic": "Safe driving"}, {"id": "parivahan-304", "category": "rules", "prompt": "Which of the following is most important when loading a vehicle?", "options": ["Loading it towards the rear", "loading it towards the front", "spreading the load evenly"], "answer": 2, "image": null, "explanation": "The published Parivahan question bank identifies “spreading the load evenly” as the correct answer.", "source_url": "https://parivahan.gov.in/sites/default/files/DownloadForm/STALL_QB_ENGLISH_NEW.pdf", "source_ref": "Question 304, PDF page 20", "imported_at": "2026-10-23", "topic": "Safe driving"}, {"id": "parivahan-305", "category": "rules", "prompt": "You are driving a tipper vehicle carrying loose dry sand. Why should you cover this load properly ?", "options": ["To stop handling being affective _x000D_", "to set your rear ward vision", "to prevent sand being blown into the eyes of other road users"], "answer": 2, "image": null, "explanation": "The published Parivahan question bank identifies “to prevent sand being blown into the eyes of other road users” as the correct answer.", "source_url": "https://parivahan.gov.in/sites/default/files/DownloadForm/STALL_QB_ENGLISH_NEW.pdf", "source_ref": "Question 305, PDF page 20", "imported_at": "2026-10-23", "topic": "Safe driving"}, {"id": "parivahan-306", "category": "rules", "prompt": "How many people can you carry over the load carried on a truck?", "options": ["one", "as per permit", "none"], "answer": 2, "image": null, "explanation": "The published Parivahan question bank identifies “none” as the correct answer.", "source_url": "https://parivahan.gov.in/sites/default/files/DownloadForm/STALL_QB_ENGLISH_NEW.pdf", "source_ref": "Question 306, PDF page 20", "imported_at": "2026-10-23", "topic": "Safe driving"}, {"id": "parivahan-307", "category": "rules", "prompt": "What should be checked first before turning to the left?", "options": ["the right side mirror", "the left side mirror", "look behind over your right shoulders"], "answer": 1, "image": null, "explanation": "The published Parivahan question bank identifies “the left side mirror” as the correct answer.", "source_url": "https://parivahan.gov.in/sites/default/files/DownloadForm/STALL_QB_ENGLISH_NEW.pdf", "source_ref": "Question 307, PDF page 20", "imported_at": "2026-10-23", "topic": "Safe driving"}, {"id": "parivahan-308", "category": "rules", "prompt": "You are about to move off you should always", "options": ["using your mirrors look behind and give proper signal", "signal left with indicator and move", "use only the off side mirror and move away quickly"], "answer": 0, "image": null, "explanation": "The published Parivahan question bank identifies “using your mirrors look behind and give proper signal” as the correct answer.", "source_url": "https://parivahan.gov.in/sites/default/files/DownloadForm/STALL_QB_ENGLISH_NEW.pdf", "source_ref": "Question 308, PDF page 20", "imported_at": "2026-10-23", "topic": "Safe driving"}, {"id": "parivahan-310", "category": "rules", "prompt": "The turning circle of a vehicle is the", "options": ["number of turns of the steering wheels between locked", "amount by which a vehicle cuts 